text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures get -2/-2 until end of turn.', 'Arcane Sanctum enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}, {U}, or {B}.', 'Artifact spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nDestroy target creature.', 'At the beginning of your end step, if you control a creature with power 5 or greater, you may draw a card.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'At the beginning of your end step, if you control a creature with power 5 or greater, you may gain 2 life.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'At the beginning of your end step, if you control a creature with power 5 or greater, you may have Exuberant Firestoker deal 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, create a 1/1 red Goblin creature token with haste.\\nGoblin creatures attack each combat if able.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, each player discards a card.', "Blightning deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker. That player or that planeswalker's controller discards two cards.", 'Change the target of target spell with a single target.', 'Choose five permanents you control. For each of those permanents, you may search your library for a card with the same name as that permanent. Put those cards onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Choose one or both —\\n• Branching Bolt deals 3 damage to target creature with flying.\\n• Branching Bolt deals 3 damage to target creature without flying.', "Choose one —\\n• Destroy target artifact.\\n• Put target creature on the bottom of its owner's library.\\n• Counter target instant spell.", 'Choose one —\\n• Destroy target enchantment.\\n• Draw two cards.\\n• Target player discards two cards.', "Choose one —\\n• Exile target player's graveyard.\\n• Jund Charm deals 2 damage to each creature.\\n• Put two +1/+1 counters on target creature.", "Choose one —\\n• Naya Charm deals 3 damage to target creature.\\n• Return target card from a graveyard to its owner's hand.\\n• Tap all creatures target player controls.", "Choose one —\\n• Return target permanent to its owner's hand.\\n• Target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.\\n• Creatures you control get +2/+0 until end of turn.", 'Count the number of cards in your library. Your life total becomes that number.', 'Counter target spell that targets you or a permanent you control.\\nDraw a card.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Counter target spell.', 'Counter target spell. Its controller loses 3 life and you gain 3 life.', 'Create two 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', "Creatures you control gain shroud until end of turn. (They can't be the targets of spells or abilities.)", 'Crumbling Necropolis enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}, {B}, or {R}.', 'Cycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Cycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nUnearth {1}{B} ({1}{B}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nExalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)", 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact or land.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Destroy three target permanents.', 'Devour 1 (As this enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures. This creature enters the battlefield with that many +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nWhen Caldera Hellion enters the battlefield, it deals 3 damage to each creature.', 'Devour 1 (As this enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures. This creature enters the battlefield with that many +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nWhen Skullmulcher enters the battlefield, draw a card for each creature it devoured.', 'Devour 2 (As this enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures. This creature enters the battlefield with twice that many +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token for each +1/+1 counter on Mycoloth.', 'Devour 2 (As this enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures. This creature enters the battlefield with twice that many +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nWhen Tar Fiend enters the battlefield, target player discards a card for each creature it devoured.', 'Devour 2 (As this enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures. This creature enters the battlefield with twice that many +1/+1 counters on it.)\\n{G}: Thorn-Thrash Viashino gains trample until end of turn.', 'Devour 3 (As this enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures. This creature enters the battlefield with three times that many +1/+1 counters on it.)', 'Dragon creatures you control get +3/+3.', 'Each creature card in your graveyard has unearth {2}{B}. ({2}{B}: Return the card to the battlefield. The creature gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', "Each player who has cast a nonartifact spell this turn can't cast additional nonartifact spells.", "Enchant artifact or creature\\nEnchanted permanent doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+0 and has trample.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+0 and has first strike. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', "Enchant creature\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, that creature's controller loses life equal to its toughness.", 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land is a Mountain, Forest, and Plains.', 'Equipped creature has deathtouch.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, that player loses half their life, rounded up.\\nEquip {3}', 'Exalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Exalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever a creature you control attacks alone, it gains double strike until end of turn.', 'Exalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever a creature you control attacks alone, you may tap target creature.', "Exalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\n{U}: Sighted-Caste Sorcerer gains shroud until end of turn. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Exalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\n{W}, {T}: Dawnray Archer deals 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', 'Exile target attacking creature.\\nCycling {5}{G}{W}{U} ({5}{G}{W}{U}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Resounding Silence, exile up to two target attacking creatures.', 'Exile target card from a graveyard. You gain 3 life.', 'Exile the top five cards of your library. An opponent separates those cards into two piles. You may play lands and cast spells from one of those piles. If you cast a spell this way, you cast it without paying its mana cost.', 'Feral Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{3}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Feral Hydra. Any player may activate this ability.', 'First strike\\nExalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', "First strike\\nShroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'First strike\\nUnearth {U}{B}{R} ({U}{B}{R}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'First strike\\nWhen Knight of the White Orchid enters the battlefield, if an opponent controls more lands than you, you may search your library for a Plains card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'First strike\\nWhenever another creature dies, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Rockslide Elemental.', 'Flash\\n{B}, {T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Draw a card.', 'Flying', "Flying, haste\\nAt the beginning of the end step, sacrifice Hell's Thunder.\\nUnearth {4}{R} ({4}{R}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)", 'Flying, haste\\nDevour 2 (As this enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures. This creature enters the battlefield with twice that many +1/+1 counters on it.)', 'Flying, trample, haste\\n{R}: Hellkite Overlord gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{B}{G}: Regenerate Hellkite Overlord.', 'Flying, trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice a non-Zombie creature, then create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', "Flying, vigilance\\nPlayers can't untap more than one creature during their untap steps.", 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your end step, you gain 3 life if Sphinx Sovereign is untapped. Otherwise, each opponent loses 3 life.', 'Flying\\nDeathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Flying\\nExalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Flying\\nExalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever a creature you control attacks alone, it gains lifelink until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nSacrifice Gustrider Exuberant: Creatures you control with power 5 or greater gain flying until end of turn.', "Flying\\nShroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\nAll damage that would be dealt to you is dealt to Empyrial Archangel instead.", 'Flying\\nUnearth {2}{U} ({2}{U}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'Flying\\nWhen Broodmate Dragon enters the battlefield, create a 4/4 red Dragon creature token with flying.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sanctum Gargoyle enters the battlefield, you may return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sharuum the Hegemon enters the battlefield, you may return target artifact card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Flying\\nWhen Welkin Guide enters the battlefield, target creature gets +2/+2 and gains flying until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Flameblast Dragon attacks, you may pay {X}{R}. If you do, Flameblast Dragon deals X damage to any target.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Sedraxis Specter deals combat damage to a player, that player discards a card.\\nUnearth {1}{B} ({1}{B}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'Flying\\nWhenever an artifact creature you control deals combat damage to a player, you may create a 1/1 blue Thopter artifact creature token with flying.', 'Flying\\nWhenever another artifact enters the battlefield under your control, Glaze Fiend gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhenever another creature dies, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Scavenger Drake.', 'Flying\\n{1}{W}: Cloudheath Drake gains vigilance until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Regenerate Skeletal Kathari.', 'Flying\\n{R}, {T}: Vein Drinker deals damage equal to its power to target creature. That creature deals damage equal to its power to Vein Drinker.\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Vein Drinker this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Vein Drinker.', 'Haste', 'Haste\\n{T}: Target creature with power 5 or greater gains haste until end of turn.', "If a creature would enter the battlefield under an opponent's control this turn, it enters the battlefield under your control instead.", 'If you would lose the game, instead shuffle your hand, your graveyard, and all permanents you own into your library, then draw seven cards and your life total becomes 20.', 'Indestructible\\n{1}: Target creature with power 5 or greater gains indestructible until end of turn.', "Jhessian Infiltrator can't be blocked.", 'Jungle Shrine enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}, {G}, or {W}.', 'Lifelink', 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)\\nWindwright Mage has flying as long as an artifact card is in your graveyard.', 'Look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal a creature card and/or a land card from among them and put the revealed cards into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Magma Spray deals 2 damage to target creature. If that creature would die this turn, exile it instead.', "Master of Etherium's power and toughness are each equal to the number of artifacts you control.\\nOther artifact creatures you control get +1/+1.", "Menace (This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\nDeathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)", "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", "Play with the top card of your library revealed.\\nAs long as the top card of your library is an artifact or creature card, Skill Borrower has all activated abilities of that card. (If any of the abilities use that card's name, use this creature's name instead.)", "Players can't search libraries.", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Put X +1/+1 counters on target creature, where X is that creature's power.", "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nExalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Reach\\nIf a creature is attacking you and you control a Forest and a Plains, you may cast Qasali Ambusher without paying its mana cost and as though it had flash.', 'Resounding Thunder deals 3 damage to any target.\\nCycling {5}{B}{R}{G} ({5}{B}{R}{G}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Resounding Thunder, it deals 6 damage to any target.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand. Its controller draws a card.", "Return target permanent to its owner's hand.\\nCycling {5}{W}{U}{B} ({5}{W}{U}{B}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Resounding Wave, return two target permanents to their owners' hands.", 'Reveal the top card of your library and put that card into your hand. You lose life equal to its mana value. You may repeat this process any number of times.', "Reveal the top three cards of your library. Target opponent may choose to put those cards into your hand. If they don't, put those cards into your graveyard and draw five cards.", 'Sacrifice Bloodpyre Elemental: It deals 4 damage to target creature. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'Savage Lands enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}, {R}, or {G}.', 'Seaside Citadel enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}, {W}, or {U}.', "Shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\nWhenever another creature dies, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Algae Gharial.", 'Sigil of Distinction enters the battlefield with X charge counters on it.\\nEquipped creature gets +1/+1 for each charge counter on Sigil of Distinction.\\nEquip—Remove a charge counter from Sigil of Distinction.', 'Skeletonize deals 3 damage to target creature. When a creature dealt damage this way dies this turn, create a 1/1 black Skeleton creature token with "{B}: Regenerate this creature."', 'Skeletons you control and other Zombies you control get +1/+1 and have deathtouch.', "Steelclad Serpent can't attack unless you control another artifact.", 'Tap an untapped creature you control: Topan Ascetic gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains double strike until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.\\nCycling {5}{R}{G}{W} ({5}{R}{G}{W}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Resounding Roar, target creature gets +6/+6 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -3/-0 until end of turn.\\nTarget creature gets -0/-3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to any target.', 'Target opponent sacrifices a creature, discards three cards, then loses 5 life. You return a creature card from your graveyard to your hand, draw three cards, then gain 5 life.', 'Target player discards a card at random.\\nCycling {5}{U}{B}{R} ({5}{U}{B}{R}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Resounding Scream, target player discards two cards at random.', 'Target player gains 7 life and draws two cards.', 'Trample', 'Trample\\nExalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Unearth {B} ({B}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'Until end of turn, creatures you control get +5/+5 and gain first strike, trample, and lifelink.', 'Until end of turn, target creature you control gets +3/+3 and other creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Vigilance, haste', 'Vigilance\\n{T}: Add {G}.', "Vigilance\\n{T}: Create an 8/8 Beast creature token that's red, green, and white.", 'When Blister Beetle enters the battlefield, target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'When Carrion Thrash dies, you may pay {2}. If you do, return another target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Corpse Connoisseur enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a creature card, put that card into your graveyard, then shuffle.\\nUnearth {3}{B} ({3}{B}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'When Elvish Visionary enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Fleshbag Marauder enters the battlefield, each player sacrifices a creature.', "When Kederekt Leviathan enters the battlefield, return all other nonland permanents to their owners' hands.\\nUnearth {6}{U} ({6}{U}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)", 'When Knight-Captain of Eos enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.\\n{W}, Sacrifice a Soldier: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', "When Oblivion Ring enters the battlefield, exile another target nonland permanent.\\nWhen Oblivion Ring leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Ranger of Eos enters the battlefield, you may search your library for up to two creature cards with mana value 1 or less, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', "When Realm Razer enters the battlefield, exile all lands.\\nWhen Realm Razer leaves the battlefield, return the exiled cards to the battlefield tapped under their owners' control.", 'When Scourge Devil enters the battlefield, creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nUnearth {2}{R} ({2}{R}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'When Sprouting Thrinax dies, create three 1/1 green Saproling creature tokens.', "When Tidehollow Sculler enters the battlefield, target opponent reveals their hand and you choose a nonland card from it. Exile that card.\\nWhen Tidehollow Sculler leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to its owner's hand.", "Whenever a creature dies, you may have Vicious Shadows deal damage to target player equal to the number of cards in that player's hand.", 'Whenever a creature with power 5 or greater enters the battlefield under your control, you may have Where Ancients Tread deal 5 damage to any target.', 'Whenever a creature with power 5 or greater enters the battlefield under your control, you may put two +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {2}. If you do, create a token that\'s a copy of that creature, except it has haste and "At the beginning of the end step, sacrifice this permanent."', 'Whenever a permanent an opponent controls is put into a graveyard, put that card onto the battlefield under your control unless that opponent pays 3 life.', 'Whenever a player taps a Mountain, Forest, or Plains for mana, that player adds one mana of any type that land produced.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, that player mills two cards.', 'Whenever another creature dies, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever another creature dies, you may have Hissing Iguanar deal 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.', "Whenever another creature dies, you may put X +1/+1 counters on Kresh the Bloodbraided, where X is that creature's power.", "Whenever you cast a spell, Manaplasm gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is that spell's mana value.", 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {1}{W}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature for each 1 life you gained.', 'Wild Nacatl gets +1/+1 as long as you control a Mountain.\\nWild Nacatl gets +1/+1 as long as you control a Plains.', "You gain life equal to target creature's power.", "You may sacrifice three artifacts rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nExile three artifact cards from your graveyard: Return Salvage Titan from your graveyard to your hand.", '[+1]: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token.\\n[+1]: Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains flying until end of turn.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "Artifacts, creatures, enchantments, and lands you control have indestructible."', '[+1]: Creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain haste until end of turn.\\n[−2]: Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn.\\n[−6]: Create five 4/4 red Dragon creature tokens with flying.', "[+1]: Target permanent doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.\\n[−2]: Ajani Vengeant deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life.\\n[−7]: Destroy all lands target player controls.", '[+1]: Untap up to two target artifacts.\\n[−X]: Search your library for an artifact card with mana value X or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\\n[−5]: Artifacts you control become artifact creatures with base power and toughness 5/5 until end of turn.', '{1}: Target creature with power 5 or greater gains first strike until end of turn.', '{1}: Target creature with power 5 or greater gains trample until end of turn.', '{1}{B}, Discard a card: Regenerate Viashino Skeleton.', "{1}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Executioner's Capsule: Destroy target nonblack creature.", "{1}{G}, Sacrifice a non-Ooze creature: Create an X/X green Ooze creature token, where X is the sacrificed creature's power. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{1}{R}: Cavern Thoctar gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "{1}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice Courier's Capsule: Draw two cards.", '{1}{W}, {T}: Prevent all damage that would be dealt to target creature with power 5 or greater this turn.', '{2}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard. Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{2}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice a blue creature, a black creature, and a red creature: Search your library for a card named Prince of Thralls, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{2}{B}: Vectis Silencers gains deathtouch until end of turn. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy that creature.)', '{2}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a red creature, a green creature, and a white creature: Search your library for a card named Godsire, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{2}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice a black creature, a red creature, and a green creature: Search your library for a card named Hellkite Overlord, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{2}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice a white creature, a blue creature, and a black creature: Search your library for a card named Sphinx Sovereign, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{2}{U}: Untap target artifact.', "{2}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Dispeller's Capsule: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.", '{2}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice a green creature, a white creature, and a blue creature: Search your library for a card named Empyrial Archangel, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{3}{G}: Knight of the Skyward Eye gets +3/+3 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', '{3}{R}{G}{W}, {T}: Look at the top five cards of your library. You may put a creature card with power 5 or greater from among them onto the battlefield. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', '{4}{G}: Rockcaster Platoon deals 2 damage to each creature with flying and each player.', '{4}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Protomatter Powder: Return target artifact card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', '{B}, {T}: Target player loses 1 life.\\n{G}, {T}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{G}, {T}: Target creature gains trample until end of turn.\\n{U}, {T}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', '{R}, {T}: Target creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn.\\n{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{R}: Undead Leotau gets +1/-1 until end of turn.\\nUnearth {2}{B} ({2}{B}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', '{T}, Exile two cards from your graveyard: Draw a card.\\nIf damage would be dealt to you, prevent that damage. Exile a card from your graveyard for each 1 damage prevented this way.\\nWhen there are no cards in your graveyard, you lose the game.', '{T}, Sacrifice Scourglass: Destroy all permanents except for artifacts and lands. Activate only during your upkeep.', '{T}: Add {B}, {R}, or {G}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Bant Panorama: Search your library for a basic Forest, Plains, or Island card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Esper Panorama: Search your library for a basic Plains, Island, or Swamp card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Grixis Panorama: Search your library for a basic Island, Swamp, or Mountain card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Jund Panorama: Search your library for a basic Swamp, Mountain, or Forest card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Naya Panorama: Search your library for a basic Mountain, Forest, or Plains card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {G}, {W}, or {U}.', '{T}: Add {R}, {G}, or {W}.', '{T}: Add {U}, {B}, or {R}.', '{T}: Add {W}, {U}, or {B}.', '{T}: Blood Cultist deals 1 damage to target creature.\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Blood Cultist this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Blood Cultist.', '{T}: Reveal any number of creature cards with power 5 or greater from your hand. Add {G} for each card revealed this way.', '{T}: Target player exiles a card from their graveyard.\\n{1}, Exile Relic of Progenitus: Exile all graveyards. Draw a card.', '{T}: Target player loses 1 life.', '{T}: Target player mills a card.', '{T}: Vithian Stinger deals 1 damage to any target.\\nUnearth {1}{R} ({1}{R}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', '{T}: You gain 1 life.', '{T}: You may tap or untap another target permanent.\\nUnearth {U} ({U}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', '{U}, {T}: Create a 0/1 blue Homunculus artifact creature token.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice a Homunculus.', "{U}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\n{R}, {T}: Target creature can't block this turn.", "{U}: Shore Snapper gains islandwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", '{U}{B}, {T}: Target player loses 1 life and reveals their hand.', '{W}, {T}: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to you this turn.\\n{B}, {T}: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', '{W}, {T}: Regenerate target artifact.']
flavor: ['"A night attack will be easy. We\'ll make an air raid over the Akrasan border. Just get me some flint to light the war torches."', '"Amateurish. Nearsighted. A waste of my time and everyone else\'s."\\n—Indra, nullmage of Vectis', '"Aven bandits can be sly. You\'ve got to fill the sky with boulders—and then seek cover immediately."\\n—Knight-Captain Wyhorn', '"By the time I got there, the heart had stopped. Fortunately, I was able to replace it with something better."', '"Esper, like any work of art, can be truly appreciated only from a distance."\\n—Tezzeret', '"Even in single combat, I am never alone."\\n—Rafiq of the Many', '"For unwavering commitment and unflinching strength, the Order of the White Orchid confers its sigil. Rise, knight-captain, and do your duty."', '"Forget. Only then will there be space for hope between the pain and fear."', '"From the highest towers to the deepest sea, all life must be touched by etherium."\\n—Lodus of the Ethersworn', '"Gargantuans die not in moments but in moons. There is still time to aid this noble ancient."', '"Give me your memories, and you will have release from the suffering they bring you."', '"I feel the vine-rhythm as my friends drive the beast to me. I will not miss my mark."', '"I find its symmetry pleasing. It rids our world of offensive refuse while disposing of itself."\\n—Dolomarus, Proctor of the Clean', '"I have trained in all three schools of magic."', '"It is sacrilege to confine a gargantuan to the grinding of straight lines. I will pray that it remembers who is the master of this land."\\n—Syeena, elvish godtoucher', '"It\'s free to do whatever it wants. I\'ve merely told it what that is."\\n—Xorin, Architect of Will', '"Jund is a wounded world. Beware its searing blood spilling out onto the surface."\\n—Rakka Mar', '"Lay sacrifice to the godsire that it may spare us, but save some for his progeny who also will hunger."\\n—Syeena, elvish godtoucher', '"Lightning lives in everything, in living flesh and growing things. It must be set free."\\n—Rakka Mar', '"Magic cast through a hand of flesh is just as weak as the flesh itself."\\n—Lodus of the Ethersworn', '"May these deaths be the first of many."', '"Mine is an insatiable god, with appetites as magnificent as the jungle itself."', '"Momentum is a great ally."', '"Never subtle nor cryptic is the reckoning of the mighty."\\n—Mayael the Anima', '"Of your blood I will make my mead, an offering to the thirsty jungle."', '"On our thirty-fourth day of digging, we unearthed a chamber that contained the intact remains of several species long extinct from Grixis. One in particular should make a fine siege engine . . . ."\\n—Last notes of Shungus Nod, fleshcrafter', '"Only a mind unfettered with the concerns of the flesh can see the world as it truly is."', '"Only by the bravery of those who put loyalty above glory is our home kept safe."\\n—Elspeth', '"Only those with the strength to seize their destiny deserve to have one."\\n—Nacatl scratchforms', '"Retribution is best delivered by claws and rage, with both magnified."\\n—Ajani', '"So many choices. Shall I choose loathing, hate, or malice today?"\\n—Eliza of the Keep', '"Soon I will sleep, eyes closing to a world tarnished with flesh, and then wake to a polished vision."\\n—Sharuum', '"Speculation is foolish when the tools of certainty are available."\\n—Cinna, vedalken consul', '"The Cloud Nacatl sit and think, a bunch of soft paws. We are the Claws of Marisi, stalking, pouncing, drawing blood."', '"The Filigree Texts do not compel you to act in accordance with their precepts. They only specify the consequences should you fail."\\n—Lodus of the Ethersworn', '"The bones of allies grant wisdom. The bones of enemies grant strength. The bones of dragons grant life eternal."', '"The dragon has no pretense of compassion, no false mask of civilization—just hunger, heat, and need."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"The dragon is a perfect marriage of power and the will to use it."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"The elves claim the canopy. The nacatl claim the mountains. I suppose you think we ought to stay on the jungle floor?"', '"The future is a snake, devouring your life backwards through time. And when you die, believe me, it doesn\'t stop feeding."\\n—Sedris, the Traitor King', '"The noble work of our order is to infuse all life on Esper with etherium. Our goal will be reached more rapidly if new life is . . . suppressed."', '"There are none alive that I cannot crush. There are none dead that I do not command."', '"There is no such thing as scrap metal. All such material can be repaired with the proper bonding agent."\\n—Quennus, metallurgeon', '"They say the ruins of Sedraxis were once a shining capital in Vithia. Now it is a blight, a place to be avoided by the living."\\n—Olcot, Rider of Joffik', '"This is going to hurt a lot, but on the bright side, you\'ll be dead soon."\\n—Sedris, the Traitor King', '"This is why we don\'t go out in banewasp weather."\\n—Rannon, Vithian holdout', '"Those may be the squirms of one life ending or of another beginning. Either way, I\'d leave it alone."\\n—Rakka Mar', '"Those talons really dig into your skin, but it\'s better than being dropped."\\n—Rafiq of the Many', '"Thoughts are commodities. Someone will pay a good price for them. Even ones as simplistic as yours . . ."\\n—Ennor, mentalist', '"Thrashes of the ancient past still linger in spirit and shadow, desperate to sink their claws into our souls."\\n—Rakka Mar', '"To immortality."', '"We can\'t beat the necromancers in numbers or raw power. We must beat them with ingenuity and timing."\\n—Rannon, Vithian holdout', '"We must rely on our own knowledge, not on the dogma of the seekers or the mutterings of the sphinxes."\\n—Tullus of Palandius', '"We of the Sanctum Arcanum have pondered every word on every page of the Filigree Texts. If you can\'t say the same, don\'t bother speaking."', '"What rises without legs, whispers without a voice, bites without teeth, and dies without having life?"', '"What you are attempting is not against the law. It is, however, extremely foolish."', '"Words are a waste of time. Destruction is a language everyone understands."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', 'A circle of light and a word of confinement.', "A dragon's death is almost as feared as its life. Old, dying dragons throw themselves into volcanoes, causing massive upheaval and widespread disaster.", 'A goblin raid is a delicate gambit—a blend of stealth, precision, and screaming death.', 'A permanent storm rages over the plain of Cloudheath, and drakes ride its currents—two reminders that some elements of Esper will not be controlled.', 'Agents of the Architects of Will mark their victims as a reminder that their secrets are secret no longer.', 'Although the Anima herself remains at the Sacellum, her druids roam Naya, collecting mana bonds with every location in the world.', 'An avatar he sculpts of anger and flame.', 'An avatar he sculpts of fellowship and light.', 'An avatar he sculpts of instinct and force.', 'As their supplies of etherium dwindled, mechanists sent gargoyles farther and farther afield in search of salvage.', 'At his side, humble beasts become weapons more deadly than sharpened steel.', 'At sea, the Jhessian fleet strikes swiftly and decisively. On land, facing the elite cavalry of Valeron, its marines must rely on more cautious strategies.', 'Bant is a world where death and chaos hold no sway.', "Bant's armies are primarily composed of members of the Mortar caste, loyal commoners who haven't yet earned a sigil.", "Bant's hearts are as pure as its air and as bright as its skies.", 'Bantians believe those who are born into the highest caste and live a life of discipline and virtue can ascend to become angels.', 'Be worthy of a single blessing, and many more will follow.', 'Before any major undertaking, a Cylian elf seeks the guidance of a visionary to learn the will of the gargantuan ancients.', 'Before signing anything on Grixis, always read the fine print.', 'Before the zealots of the Ethersworn came to power, Esper illusionists dreamed up creations to mimic a variety of substances.', "Between the thunderous footfalls of Naya's behemoths lie moments of perfect quiet.", 'Bloated with venom, it crawls Grixis looking for victims to ooze onto.', 'Both guide and guard on open plain.', 'Centuries have passed since the plane shattered, yet the obelisks of each shard faithfully serve their long-forgotten purpose.', 'Centuries of careful practice have elevated the casting of protective spells to an art form. What little offensive magic remains on Bant stands little chance of breaching them.', 'Clash of sword and cry of beast fall mute when angels sound the call to prayer.', "Deep in nature's core lies a potential unsullied by greed or civilization.", 'Dragon lords of Jund rule by edicts of flame.', 'Dragons consider drakes to be mockeries of their perfection, destroying them on sight.', 'Dragons make for spiteful gods.', 'Each mutation causes the incurables to look vastly different from one another. They are left with only one thing in common: their insatiable lust for the slaughter.', 'Each of his twenty-two braids is bound with bone and leather from a foe.', 'Each sigil marks the recognition of a great deed and signifies a duty owed to the one who granted it.', 'Elementals born of Jund are as cruel and unstable as the plane itself.', 'Elves believe the hydra-god Progenitus sleeps beneath Naya, feeding on forgotten magics.', 'Esper is an expansive canvas painted by precise, controlling hands.', 'Etherium does not know sleep. Only magic can teach it the resting state of cold steel.', 'Even on Esper, there are those who eschew the use of magic in favor of simpler methods.', 'Even the most battle-hardened soldiers pause in her presence for a moment of introspection.', "Every once in a while, when they aren't getting incinerated in lava, crushed under rock slides, or devoured by dragons, goblins experience moments of unmitigated glory in battle.", "Few Nayans dare hunt the gargantuans. They're regarded not as animals but as forces of nature, like landslides or typhoons.", 'Fire burns away both flesh and freedom.', 'For the necromancer barons, killing and recruitment are one and the same.', "For wisdom's sake, it was built high to gaze on all things. For glory's sake, it was built high as a testament of power. For strength's sake, it was built high to repel all attacks.", "From her sunsail tent high above the forest floor, an elf harkener can hear the footfalls of a single creature through the cacophony of Naya's jungle sounds.", 'Frozen in fear, the goblins stared upward at the circling hunter—and were promptly eaten by its diving mate.', "Goblin lairs sit high in Jund's mountains. This gives the goblins easy access to the sacrificial peaks above and lets them build up a head of steam before attacking prey down below.", "Goblins journey to the sacrificial peaks in pairs so that the rare survivor might be able to relate the details of the other's grisly demise.", 'Grixis is a world where the only things found in abundance are death and decay. Corpses, whole or in part, are the standard currency among necromancers and demons.', 'He bids his minions rise from their graves to their knees.', 'He calls a riddle through the gaps of cloven clouds, hoping for an answer.', 'He scowls at his imperfect creation, then crushes it to scrap. He salvages the etherium and begins anew.', 'He watches over the valley where Progenitus sleeps, culling signs from its steaming breaths.', 'Her connection to the gargantuans puts her in line to become Anima, a sacred but daunting duty.', 'Her wings are the prayers of the devoted; her sword, the despair of the vile.', 'If you breathe, she will fight you. If you breathe fire, she must fight you.', 'In ages past, Esper couriers bore messages written on ornate scrolls. The medium has grown more sophisticated, but the principle remains the same.', 'It holds motionless vigil, watching Naya in silence through the screen of the whitecover. When it senses anything amiss, it launches forward with the uncanny sound of torn fog.', 'It is a monument as austere, unyielding, and inscrutable as Esper itself.', 'It lurks just under the surface, using the algae-choked tar pits of Jund as both home and hunting blind.', 'It shows not what you are but what you were.', 'It shreds its prey as each head fights for the choicest bits.', 'Jund has little necromancy. Instead, the flesh of its dead gives rise to algal fiends.', 'Jund is a world as cruel as those who call it home. Their brutal struggles scar the land even as it carves them in its image, a vicious circle spiraling out of control.', 'Jund pulses with raw energy, waiting for shamans to shape it into useful form.', 'Kathari, the sickly aven of Grixis, have learned that the corpses by the shoreline are more trap than treat.', "Knight-stewards guard the Sun-Dappled Court, a grove of immense, sculptured olive trees that represent Valeron's twelve noble families.", "Life's circle has become inverted in Grixis. The same energy is endlessly recycled and becomes more stagnant with each pass.", 'Like most features of Grixis, the obelisks that remain from the time of Alara now exist only for dark exploitation.', 'Many sigils, one purpose.', 'Monks from Topa wander all of Bant, encouraging the Unbeholden to find their place in society through honorable combat.', "Natives of Naya know better than to loiter near the mouth of a cave. Two glowing red eyes and the stench of foul breath are all the warning you're likely to get.", 'Naya teems with gargantuans, titanic monsters to whom both nature and civilization defer.', "Naya's bounty spills over upon itself. Each leaf and flower struggles against the next with thrashing thorns, acidic pollen, and strangling roots.", "Naya's celebrants stoke the gargantuans into a rage, loosing a tide of muscle with the precision of an arrow.", "Naya's trees grow tall and sturdy. Their foliage intertwines to form dewcups, rainwater pools where the elves gather to celebrate life.", 'On Bant, a sigil is both a prize of honor and a bond of duty. The one who bears it may be called to fulfill that charge at any moment.', 'On Jund, even the landscape is a deadly hunter. Volcanoes, tar pits, and rock slides seem to prey upon the living.', 'On Naya, ambition and treachery are scarce, hunted nearly to extinction by the awe owed to terrestrial gods.', "Once a year, Akrasa holds a joust that draws knights and their leotaus from every nation on Bant. The prize is an Akrasan sigil, but the true reward is the angel's kiss.", 'One of the most ferocious and deadly gargantuans, the thoctar never sees its worshippers, but it often awakens surrounded by gifts and sacrifices.', "Rebels and other malcontents forced into the ritual awake lost in Topa's vast savannahs. Those who find their way back return humble and repentant.", "Revealing the truth only deepened Tezzeret's curiosity for the secrets still buried.", 'Rhox monks are dedicated to spiritual growth and learning, and most bear the sigils of many students. However, they do not gladly suffer fools or those who disagree with their carefully wrought dogma.', 'Rigorous faith and belief are rewarded on occasion, and richly so.', 'Rogue mechanists once rummaged through the wastes of the Tidehollow, constructing unauthorized golems to threaten the hegemony of the sphinxes. The orbs put a stop to that.', 'She can heal the flesh, or exploit its many weaknesses.', "She knows the names and secrets of each of Esper's twenty-three winds.", 'She stands ready, always watchful, knowing that weeks of peace and serenity can be overturned by a single distant sail.', 'Some Serul Cove rogues traffic in stolen sigils, which fetch a high price from those who would rather pay for honor than earn it.', "Some believe the spiky crystal called sangrite is concentrated dragon's breath. Others think it's crystallized life energy. The clans care only about the power it unleashes when crushed.", 'Sunseeders quest for areas of open sky. They train plowbeasts to beat back the dense jungle long enough to cultivate a crop.', "The Jhessian navy makes successful raids on Valeron's coastal towns thanks to their spies planted during peacetime.", 'The Order of the Skyward Eye does the bidding of an evil force, unwittingly stirring fear and mistrust across Bant in accordance with his plans.', 'The Sun-Dappled Court of Valeron stands secure behind a wall of steel-tipped arrows.', "The artistry of Etlan's firedancers is more spectacular when behemoths join in.", 'The behemoth roared, and the world was blasted free of empires and tyrants.', 'The consuming undeath of Grixis terrifies the survivors of Vithia, but its fauna is just as fearsome.', "The cup was a gift from the sphinx Tameron, who hoped that those who drank from it would live long enough to decrypt the sphinxes' wisdom.", 'The goblet was a gift from the sphinx Gorael, who hoped humans and vedalken would eventually destroy each other to acquire it, leaving all of Esper to her own kind.', 'The greatest gift you can give a sea aven is solitude.', 'The greatest masters of the craft abandon tools altogether, shaping metal with hand and mind alone.', 'The idols of old are rich in minerals and magic. They are torn apart when nature aims to eat well.', 'The island nation of Jhess is under constant siege from Valeron on the mainland. Riders traverse the coastline, always on the lookout for sails or aven.', 'The necropolis at Unx was once a living city, its streets untrodden by death.', 'The penultimate step of the ritual involves bathing in a delicious glaze.', "The sacred Anima's eyes are blind to all but the grandest truths.", 'The scullers beneath Esper keep strixes as trained pets, and set them loose when a fare refuses to pay.', "The sky is the dragon's throne, the seat from which it issues its fiery decrees.", "The strength of Bant's caste system is the unfailing loyalty of its meekest members.", 'The surprise of a battle cry can be as deadly as a blade.', 'The undead of Grixis are fueled by their hatred of the living.', 'The vast network of predation on Jund has actually caused some strange creatures to adapt to being eaten.', "Their shots are fired most often as signals—or at those who didn't get the message.", 'There is always a greater power.', 'There is always a moment of trepidation before opening a message capsule, for fear of the judgment that might be contained within.', 'There is no height above Grixis that is free from the stench of death.', 'To crack a mirror is to provide an opening for the reflection to escape.', 'To gain audience with the hegemon, one must bring a riddle she has not heard.', "Undeath doesn't end the kathari's search for carrion; it only removes one corpse from the Dregscape.", 'Underneath the Dregscape lay the remains of creatures long extinct from Grixis.', 'Urak froze when he heard it. That was his first mistake. He turned and cast a dramatic ward spell. That was his last.', 'Viashino hunt in gangs called thrashes. Not all thrashes hunt the freshest game.', 'Viashino thrashes are led by elders who have survived countless challenges.', 'Viashino thrashes keep iguanars as hunting companions, giving them wounded captives as playthings.', 'Vitals of Grixis who eschew undeath must scrape and scratch to retain their mortality. The result is a breed of inventive mages.', 'Volcanic ash-winds batter it, climbing vines overwhelm it, dragonfire roasts it, and yet it still stands as a testament to a forgotten world.', 'Warriors of the Rip Clan wear their beetle-acid scars proudly, even modifying clothing and armor to better display the trophy.', "Weavers' webs wall off swaths of territory more effectively than any portcullis made of iron.", "When the task spilled over into undeath, he stopped calling it his life's work.", 'Whether gargantuans are the manifested will of Progenitus or simply the result of overabundant resources is moot when a herd of them is thundering at you.', "Whether incorporated into the structure of castles or admired as lone symbols, the obelisks stand for Bant's values of loyalty, honor, and truth.", 'Whether mechanical or biological, life finds a way to propagate itself.', 'While the smell of burning flesh is common in Grixis, the odor of smoldering brain matter is a rare treat.', 'Why settle for mere enormity?', 'Witches of the Split-Eye Coven speak of a future when Grixis will overflow with life energy. For now, they must harvest vis from the living to fuel their dark magics.']
artist: ['Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Andrew Murray', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Ash Wood', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cole Eastburn', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Daarken', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Dan Seagrave', 'Dave Allsop', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'Dominick Domingo', 'Donato Giancola', 'E. M. Gist', 'Francis Tsai', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Greg Staples', 'Hideaki Takamura', 'Howard Lyon', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jarreau Wimberly', 'Jason Chan', 'Jean-Sébastien Rossbach', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jon Foster', 'Joshua Hagler', 'Justin Sweet', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Mark Brill', 'Mark Hyzer', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Meel Tamphanon', 'Michael Bruinsma', 'Michael Komarck', 'Michael Ryan', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mitch Cotie', 'Nils Hamm', 'Paolo Parente', 'Paul Bonner', 'Pete Venters', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Sal Villagran', 'Shelly Wan', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
